    "body": "## Summary\n- centralize public job discovery in a viewer-aware `JobDiscoveryService`\n- exclude jobs across symmetric user blocks directly in paginated and geospatial database queries\n- apply the same database-level block filtering to private saved-search radius results\n- preserve anonymous public discovery behavior when there is no authenticated viewer\n- remove the superseded nearby-discovery service so there is only one policy-aware discovery path\n- add regression coverage for authenticated/anonymous discovery, category normalization and saved-search viewer filtering\n- update `USER_BLOCKING.md`\n\n## Privacy / correctness\n- reverse-block state is never exposed to clients\n- blocked jobs are filtered before pagination, distance ordering and LIMIT, so totals and nearby result slots stay correct\n- exact locations, routes, live tracking, escrow and participant lifecycle authorization are unchanged\n- no new migration is required; filtering reuses the existing indexed `user_blocks` relationship\n\n## Validation\nRun backend Maven verify, frontend lint/build and applicable runtime smoke workflows. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
